    "q-95265": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95265",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x$ for $|x|<1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
